    {
      "id": "claim_d30116e1337d466fb25f67b09ffa65a7",
      "statement": "_setup_portal_session() talks to org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop / org.freedesktop.portal.ScreenCast over a pydbus SessionBus; each of CreateSession, SelectSources, and Start blocks a GLib.MainLoop that quits on the portal Request Response signal (with a 30-second timeout guard). CreateSession options include a timestamp-suffixed session_handle_token, persist_mode=2 (persist consent until explicitly revoked), and the saved restore_token only when non-empty. SelectSources uses types=1 for whole screen or 2 for a specific window with multiple=false; Start returns the PipeWire node id and possibly a fresh restore_token.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/capture.py#L239-L391",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9d3b0f107e512c0e98b45bddb091ae35ac7841a91a7549e45947b4c11dbf1b5a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_161b996d40cb4971ae0d2fe036c26fb5",
      "statement": "Portal restore tokens implement persistent screen-share consent: the class exposes set_on_restore_token_changed(callback) and AppContext wires it to settings.capture.restore_token plus save(), so a token issued after consent is persisted and replayed in CreateSession on later runs to skip the permission dialog. In capture(), if session setup fails while a cached token is in use, the token is cleared (callback fired with empty string, which AppContext persists) and session setup is retried once without it to force a fresh permission dialog; hosts that issue no token (pre-GNOME-47 / pre-Plasma-6) are told the prompt will recur each sync.",
      "evidence": [
