    {
      "id": "claim_0ca7e5bd7ce34ee38c5eeecdb0a4cfeb",
      "statement": "_start_pipeline() iterates the candidates, treating a set_state(PLAYING) FAILURE as 'mark config and try next'; when a running pipeline later emits a bus error, _on_pipeline_error adds the active config to _runtime_failed_configs (a set of keys produced by _config_key(), which strips path=/width=/height= values from the pipeline string so the key is stable across node ids and dimensions), stops the pipeline, and future starts skip remembered configs until stop_pipeline() clears the set. A scale-factor or frame-size change while running triggers _restart_pipeline(), which stops and re-runs the candidate loop.",
