    {
      "id": "claim_ca7dcbc9900943a08101a87576cfb597",
      "statement": "Frame extraction takes the raw mapped buffer bytes plus a stride taken from GstVideo.buffer_get_video_meta(buffer).stride[0] when available (otherwise inferred from buffer size, since GStreamer pads rows to alignment boundaries); _extract_pixel_rows validates the buffer size and, when padded, builds a strided numpy view via np.lib.stride_tricks.as_strided and .copy() to detach from the mapped buffer. A failed buffer.map(READ) is logged as the DMA-BUF signature with the hint to install GStreamer GL plugins (gst-plugins-gl).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/capture.py#L597-L660",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b886fa88cb0401d257d765e5ae55845186a597aadbebc88b55dff34366c7c5f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c46520e061f648608360702da60d6f3a",
      "statement": "_on_new_sample converts each frame to an HxWx3 (or HxWx4) uint8 array per format: BGR is flipped and copied, RGBA/RGBx are kept as 4 channels, BGRA/BGRx have channel order rearranged to RGBA, 15-bit RGB15/BGR15 are unpacked from a uint16 view with 5-bit to 8-bit scaling, and anything else is assumed RGB; the result plus the raw bytes are stored under a frame lock.",
      "evidence": [
