          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/capture.py#L660-L708",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:226f998c201383e7fa58897d37d543c9580fe7e749ef20146d0222e51e52d814:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2a55c790168c42d887f23a2f283a6170",
      "statement": "_process_image applies the black-bar crop region when a detector is attached, then scales with PIL bilinear only when the pipeline itself is not already emitting scaled frames (a C-contiguous copy is made first); update_scale_factor() clamps to [0.01, 1.0] and restarts the running pipeline when the computed target dimensions actually change, preferring pipeline-side scaling over a second full-frame CPU resize.",
