    {
      "id": "claim_4669135345f3417d8cf272edbb33ddbd",
      "statement": "BlackBarDetector computes BT.601 luma (0.299R + 0.587G + 0.114B) directly on the numpy array, reduces to row/column mean luminance, and walks in from each edge counting contiguous lines whose mean is at or below threshold (default 10, clamped 0-50); detection runs every detection_rate frames (default 30, clamped 1-120) and the returned crop lerps toward the target at smooth_factor (default 0.3, clamped 0.1-1.0). Guards: an axis is reset if cropping would leave less than 50% content, each edge is capped at dim//2-1, degenerate crops re-expand to the full frame, any exception resets to no-crop, and _should_crop suppresses cropping unless the crop differs from the full frame by more than 2% in either dimension.",
      "evidence": [
